# supercronic reads this inside the container. Six jobs share this one
# clock now (#774): the sweeper's own drain plus the five evaluated-stream/
# status pollers this issue moved off GitHub Actions `schedule:` — which
# delivered them roughly once every four hours (#773's measurements) —
# onto the always-on clock `hummingbird-sweeper` already runs. Adding an
# entry here extends the clock supercronic already owns; it does not start
# a second one (CLAUDE.md's "No competing clocks" rule; #773 makes the
# argument in full).
#
# Each poller's cadence matches its own `POLLED_EVERY_MS` (or, for
# `github-status-poll`, `body::POLLED_EVERY_MS`): the four stream pollers
# every 15 minutes, `github-status-poll` every 30. The minute offsets are
# staggered off `/app/sweep` and off one another, deliberately — the
# machine is `shared-cpu-1x`/256mb, and six jobs landing on the same tick is
# an avoidable spike rather than a necessary one.
*/15 * * * * /app/sweep
2,17,32,47 * * * * HB_INGEST_TOKEN="$GMAIL_INGEST_TOKEN" /app/bin/hummingbird-gmail-poll
5,20,35,50 * * * * HB_INGEST_TOKEN="$CALENDAR_INGEST_TOKEN" /app/bin/hummingbird-calendar-poll
8,23,38,53 * * * * HB_INGEST_TOKEN="$M365_MAIL_INGEST_TOKEN" /app/bin/graph-mail-poll
11,26,41,56 * * * * HB_INGEST_TOKEN="$M365_CALENDAR_INGEST_TOKEN" /app/bin/graph-calendar-poll
14,44 * * * * HB_INGEST_TOKEN="$GH_STATUS_INGEST_TOKEN" GITHUB_TOKEN="$GH_STATUS_PAT" /app/bin/github-status-poll
